WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.540
Gilgamesh and Balarant.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.290
For a hundred years now,

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:42.040
these two star systems have been locked in a war
whose cause was long-forgotten.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.670
As both sides, by now exhausted,
prepared to finally end the war...

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:51.080
I was ordered into an operation
whose details were kept from me...

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:56.920
for a mysterious prize
which involved attacking an allied base.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:02.630
That day, my destiny changed. The moment I saw her...

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.210
She was apparently the military's greatest secret.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:18.210
My endless wanderings since deserting the army
had brought me to the city of Uoodo.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:27.080
And I was now in trouble with the "Boone Family."
The gang of thugs who ran the city.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:35.420
ENCOUNTER

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.630
You got that? Today we take care of them!

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:45.170
Don't leave a blade of grass unturned in the search!

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:49.420
We can't afford to have even one guy escape from here!

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.710
When we find these guys
who think they can screw with us...

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:56.630
we're gonna make an example out them.
One for everyone to see!

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.540
Oh, you came.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:22.630
No work today.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:23.710
Nothing?

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:25.670
Nothing.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:28.040
Cheh.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.040
Hey, who's this?

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.290
Got any money?

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.790
Cut it out and get lost! Shoo! Shoo!

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.250
I'll bet you're getting set for something big.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.920
Don't let your guard down!

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:02.830
That old man'll steal the hair off your butt if you let him!

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:04.500
You little...!
That old man'll steal the hair off your butt if you let him!

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:11.830
And don't come back! You damned alley cat!

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.500
You're probably hungry. Here, eat.

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:28.290
The name's Gotho.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:30.500
Chirico.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.250
You're one of the guys who broke out last night.

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.290
And it looks like you iced the guy chasing you.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:43.630
You may have survived,
but the cops and the Family are a real sweat about it.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:47.420
You must be one hell of a guy
to have escaped from there.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.080
What's with the police in this city?

00:05:55.080 --> 00:06:00.750
The security police force was formed in the confusion at
the end of the war, out of miserable excuses for soldiers.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:28.040
There they go again. Little punks!

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:32.040
Raising hell on those overgrown bikes of theirs.

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:34.580
Riding around like they own this damn town!

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.580
They're the guys who nabbed you.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:44.170
They've been working with the cops
to find miners to work the jijirium mine.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:50.880
I heard the chief of police was on the take
and let 'em get away with it, but he got killed.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:59.290
By the way, you think you might
want to help me with this pile of junk?

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:02.210
You won't find any work if you go someplace else.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.710
Would you let me have that?

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:15.420
It's totaled.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.420
I'm leaving the city.
It's totaled.

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.130
I want to fix it up and rearm it.

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:24.080
I can't let you just borrow it. Think this over.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:27.130
You won't find anyone as nice as me if you leave here.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:28.830
I'll pay you back some day.

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:32.330
The interest'll be high!

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.250
File the documents I brought with me over there.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:22.830
And get me a map that shows our jurisdiction in detail.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:25.630
What's this?

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.130
They belonged to the last chief of police.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:32.040
The dead guy?

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:32.380
Yes, sir.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:33.080
Have them burned.
Yes, sir.

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:42.210
Damn that Boone.

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:46.080
Playing like he's some big shot who runs Uoodo.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:51.580
Yes, sir. He has his goons out trying like Hell to
find the guys who escaped the mine last night.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:57.040
They're trying to take care of them before they can finger
them in the murder of the last police chief.

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:00.420
Dead men tell no tales, eh?

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:05.790
I get the feeling an escapee
was the one who killed the chief.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.080
Boone wouldn't have done it himself.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:14.170
The escapees probably did it,
and now we'll let Boone kill them off.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:19.420
Doesn't really matter what the truth is, does it?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.880
But we can't let them run things anymore.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:28.830
Uoodo doesn't need any more big shots
running around in it!

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.130
That's what I intend to do.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.790
When the time comes, we'll finish them off in one shot.

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:38.080
Until then, we stay out of it.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.670
Your heart's set on leaving?

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:09.330
With Boone's goons wandering around,
you can't drive anywhere straight!

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:12.130
Who's that? Someone you scouted out?

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:16.330
One of those guys who escaped last night.
Wandered in here.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:20.830
Used to be a VOTOM pilot.

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:25.210
Saves you the trouble of scouting one.

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:29.170
Yeah, but our guest seems to want to get outta here.

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.920
Jeez, he's got some serious stones, doesn't he?

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:36.710
I got a feeling I should keep an eye on him.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:40.130
Let him do what he wants and see exactly
what he can do for you, huh?

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:41.750
You never change.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.460
Right, that reminds me.

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:49.830
My client just wants 20 rifles this time.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:51.830
Here you go.

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:54.380
Hold on, I'll see what I've got.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:11.540
Hi!

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:15.790
The name's Vanilla. I hear you were a VOTOM jockey.

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:19.420
Wanna join up with me?
I've been looking for a guy with talent.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:23.290
Okay, you'd be working the black market...

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:27.880
But you can trust me more than the old man here.

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:30.540
These days, they say I'm as trustworthy as God!

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:33.250
See these honest eyes? Look!

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:50.830
Guy's a few rounds short of a full clip.

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:53.210
Oh, now there's a beauty!

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.960
I only have five right now.

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:58.420
I can get more tonight. You wanna come back?

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:01.540
No, that's okay. I'll stick around till tonight.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:04.540
He looks like he's gonna be at it for a while there.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:06.210
Good timing. At least I won't be bored.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:49.460
Hey, you seen one of the guys who escaped?

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:51.500
You seen anybody new in the area?

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.880
Of course, that guy.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:02.880
Has that got it?

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.880
Nah, the turret's tracking too slow to the right.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.790
So what if it's a little slow?

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:11.250
Indicate escape routes using pattern one.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:18.210
Now indicate probability of counterattack
and enemy strength along route one.

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:21.630
Show maximum enemy strength
in battlefield one situation.

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.130
Try opening the valve on the right-hand chamber!

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:39.170
What's the deal? Isn't the valve clearing all right?

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:42.630
We've got something wrong with the muscle compressor.

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:49.920
Stop! Stop!

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:52.670
Are you trying to help or to sabotage us?

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:00.710
This is hopeless!

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:04.790
You could work for two days
on this wreck and still not fix it!

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.000
The pressurization pump?

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.170
The variable compressor.

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:18.250
He's not in sector 12-K.

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.540
We checked 13-M and 13-S, too.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:22.250
Nothing in 18-E.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.500
Where the Hell is that little shit hiding?!

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:29.670
That bastard offed Horo. We can't let him live!

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:34.790
Shit... All that's left is 14-F and 15-P.

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:36.630
15-P?!

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:42.830
Rain! Move out!

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:46.880
Let's go!

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:15.170
Looks like they stopped looking
before they got to 14-F and 15-P.

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:21.250
There's only one escapee left unaccounted for.

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:24.920
He'll be the bait.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:30.130
Outside, the acid rain began to fall again.

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:37.880
The effects of the war had created a red rain which fell
almost continuously on the city and its inhabitants.

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:56.880
Hey, Kid! Why don't you relax and have a drink?

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:10.960
Didn't expect you on a night like this.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:13.960
I thought he'd still be here.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:18.790
I see you've got the booze out.

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:19.880
What's wrong?

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.630
Big big trouble.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:25.500
I know who that guy is.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:31.130
He's the last of the guys
who escaped the mine last night.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:35.710
The Family's in a big hurry to find him.

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:39.420
You live in sector 15-P, right?

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:41.960
Yeah, this is 15-P.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.920
They're coming here.

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:50.750
I heard them say they're done
looking everywhere except 14-F and 15-P.

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:55.630
I see... This rain'll last till morning at least.

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:59.670
If we don't do anything by then, we'll be in big trouble.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.250
Hey! HEY!

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:10.580
What?

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:12.830
Come on, I just gave you some prime info here!

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:15.250
You gotta give me something!

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:16.750
Here, drink this.

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:19.960
Hey, I don't even drink!

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:25.880
I didn't even tell them he was here
when those goons asked me!

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.040
Well, screw you!

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:48.580
You did it!

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:49.500
Way to go.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:50.880
But can it move?

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:54.000
I fixed it. You think it wouldn't move?

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.880
No, considering you were half-tanked when you did it.

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:03.710
Hey, Kid! Let's see what you've got.

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:09.420
So, the ulterior motive kicks in.

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:16.460
But what're the odds this piece of crap
can take on the Family?

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.250
50 gildans says it can.

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:19.080
100 gildans it can't.

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:21.080
Are you really gonna do this?

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:35.500
You won't be able to run out of here.

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:38.130
They'll find you no matter which route you take.

00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:07.420
200.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:09.250
You're on!

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:18.750
Let's go!

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.710
Why, you... Who's in that thing?

00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:27.000
What do we do?

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:28.580
Drive straight through.

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:29.580
Yes, Ma'am.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:35.500
Why, you...

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:57.380
Men! Listen to me!

00:20:58.420 --> 00:21:02.540
Today we sever our ties with the Boone Family...

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:06.130
and take control of the jijirium section ourselves!

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:10.080
Our chief objective is the annihilation of Boone's men!

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:13.830
Scramble our mobile troops and patrol teams to go to it!

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:24.500
Vulcan cannon select!

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:05.040
We've been double-crossed!

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:42.380
The flying bullets, the flames...

00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:45.670
Before my eyes lay a scene so familiar to me.

00:22:47.580 --> 00:22:49.750
I was back on the battlefield.

00:22:50.790 --> 00:22:52.460
My VOTOM and I.

00:22:53.960 --> 00:22:55.380
NEXT EPISODE

00:22:55.880 --> 00:22:59.420
Once there were grave warriors
who followed the song of battle.

00:22:59.420 --> 00:23:03.710
Here now is a graveyard
for the dignified defenders of their lands who...

00:23:03.710 --> 00:23:05.170
wrap themselves in the thick armor
of the Armored Trooper.

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:08.290
Giving entertainment to countless
Caligulas in their coliseum...

00:23:08.290 --> 00:23:11.500
they are Uoodo's gladiators.

00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:16.250
For the soulless VOTOMS themselves,
it offers the crashes that go along with their existence.

00:23:16.250 --> 00:23:18.250
Next time, "Battling"

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:22.130
From the rotating turret blazes Chirico's fierce gaze.

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:23.960
NEXT EPISODE

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:23.960
BATTLING

00:23:42.210 --> 00:23:45.670
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:45.670 --> 00:23:49.210
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:49.210 --> 00:23:55.580
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:59.630
Whenever I'm alone

00:23:59.630 --> 00:24:03.040
Whenever I long for you

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:09.290
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:09.290 --> 00:24:12.790
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:12.790 --> 00:24:16.210
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:22.710
The memories of you seem to shine inside my heart...

00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:29.040
Brighter than any other light...
